{
    "background_story": "Finn was a British explorer who traveled extensively throughout India during the 19th century. While on an expedition in the royal courts of Hyderabad, he met a kind-hearted Begum, the wife of the Nizam of Hyderabad. She was impressed by Finn's curiosity and sense of adventure, and the two formed an unlikely friendship. The Begum, fascinated by Finn's stories of the Western world, requested that he teach her about the customs and traditions of his homeland. In return, she shared with him the rich history and culture of her own people. As Finn prepared to leave India, the Begum gifted him a rare, intricately crafted silver box, adorned with the emblem of her royal family. Finn treasured the box, symbolizing the strong bond he had formed with the Begum and the people of Hyderabad.",
